          %h2#References References
          %p
            The idea of axiomatizing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            using ideas inspired by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            theory originates in
          %ul
            %li#Lawvere67
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"}> Bill Lawvere
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categorical+dynamics"} Categorical dynamics
          %p They were published as pp.1-28 in
          %ul
            %li#Kocke79
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"} Anders Kock
              (ed.):
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos+Theoretic+Methods+in+Geometry"} Topos Theoretic Methods in Geometry
              , Aarhus Univ. Var. Pub. Ser. 30 (1979).
          %p The first model for the axioms presented there served to demonstrate that the theory is non-empty, but was hard to work with. Much of the later work was concerned with refining the model-building. For instance
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eduardo+Dubuc"}> Eduardo Dubuc
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sur les modèles de la géométrie différentielle synthétique
              %strong XX-3
              (1979) pp.231-279. (
              %a{:href => "http://archive.numdam.org/article/CTGDC_1979__20_3_231_0.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            These models are constructed in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} toposes
            on the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+loci"} smooth loci
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+algebra"} C^∞-rings
          %p Transcripts or notes of further talks by Bill Lawvere on the subject are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"}> Bill Lawvere
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toposes+of+laws+of+motion"} Toposes of laws of motion
                , transcript of a talk in Montreal, Sept. 1997 (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/LawvereToposesOfLawsOfMotions.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                )
              %p
                (on the description of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential equations
                in terms of synthetic differential geometry)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"}> Bill Lawvere
                ,
                %em Outline of synthetic differential geometry
                , lectures in Buffalo (1998). (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/LawvereSDGOutline.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p An abstract of another talk which reuses the title of the original 1967 lectures and 1978 notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"}> Bill Lawvere
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mat.uc.pt/~ct2011/abstracts/lawvere_w.pdf"} Categorical Dynamics
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Category+Theory+conference"} Category Theory Conference
              2011 in Vancouver.
          %p
            Two articles that exhibit the link to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum+mechanics"} continuum mechanics
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"}> F. W. Lawvere
                ,
                %em Toward the description in a smooth topos of the dynamically possible motions and deformations of a continuous body
                , Cah. Top. Géom. Diff. Cat.
                %strong 21
                no.4 (1980) pp.377-392. (
                %a{:href => "http://archive.numdam.org/article/CTGDC_1980__21_4_377_0.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"}> F. W. Lawvere
                ,
                %em Categorical algebra for continuum microphysics
                , JPAA
                %strong 175
                (2002) pp.267-287.
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eduardo+Dubuc"} Eduardo Dubuc
              %em
                Archimedian local
                = succeed "-rings" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
              Cahiers de Topologie et Géométrie Différentielle Catégoriques,
              %strong XXVII-3
              (1986) pp.3-22. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1986__27_3_3_0"}> numdam
              ).
          %p For the early French connection see:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Weil"}> André Weil
                ,
                %em Théorie des points proches sur les variétés différentiables
                , Colloq. Top. et Géom. Diff., Strasbourg (1953) pp.111-117.
            %li
              %p
                Jean Penon,
                %em De l’infinitésimal au local (Thèse de Doctorat d’État)
                Diagrammes
                %strong S13
                (1985), pp.1-191. (
                %a{:href => "http://archive.numdam.org/article/DIA_1985__S13__1_0.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Khavkine"}> Igor Khavkine
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Synthetic+variational+calculus"} Synthetic geometry of differential equations: I. Jets and comonad structure
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.06238"}> arXiv:1701.06238
              )
          %p
            Discussion in differentially cohesive
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li#Wellen17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+Wellen"}> Felix Wellen
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/thesis+Wellen"} Formalizing Cartan Geometry in Modal Homotopy Type Theory
              (2017)
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/thesis+Wellen"} Felix's thesis work
            has finally been (submitted and thus) published:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+Cherubini"}> Felix Cherubini
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Synthetic
                    = succeed "-jet-structures" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi G
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129524000355"} doi:10.1017/S0960129524000355
            %li#JazMyers22
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Jaz+Myers"}> David Jaz Myers
                ,
                %em Orbifolds as microlinear types in synthetic differential cohesive homotopy type theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.15887"}> arXiv:2205.15887
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#books Books
          %p
            A nice elementary introduction which emphasizes calculations and the application as
            %em engineering mathematics
            can be found in
          %ul
            %li#Bell98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Lane+Bell"}> John Lane Bell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Primer of Infinitesimal Analysis
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/de/academic/subjects/mathematics/logic-categories-and-sets/primer-infinitesimal-analysis-2nd-edition?format=HB&isbn=9780521887182"} ISBN:9780521887182
          %p The textbooks
          %ul
            %li#Kock81
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Synthetic Differential Geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://users-math.au.dk/kock/sdg99.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511550812"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511550812
            %li#Kock10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Synthetic geometry of manifolds
                %strong 180
                (2010) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511691690"}> doi:10.1017/CBO9780511691690
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://tildeweb.au.dk/au76680/SGM-final.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            develop the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            using the axioms of synthetic differential geometry. The main goal in these books is to demonstrate how these axioms lead to a very elegant, very intuitive and very comprehensive conception of differential geometry. Accordingly, concrete models (whose explicit description is typically much more evolved than the nice axiomatics that holds once they have been constructed) play a minor role in these books.
          %p
            Somewhat complementary to that,
            %a{:href => "#MoerdijkReyes1991"} Moerdijk &amp; Reyes 1991
            focuse on concrete constructions of well-adapted models using the technology of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+algebra"} generalized smooth algebras
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
            \-rings).
          %p Another textbook is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ren%C3%A9+Lavendhomme"}> René Lavendhomme
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Basic concepts of synthetic differential geometry
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 13
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4757-4588-7"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4588-7
          %h3#expositions Expositions
          %p Introductory survey includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Synthetic differential geometry - new methods for old spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/New+Spaces+for+Mathematics+and+Physics"} New Spaces for Mathematics and Physics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AXz7xu3WrPE"} video recording
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
                ,
                %em New methods for old spaces: synthetic differential geometry
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.00286"}> arxiv/1610.00286
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Introductory expositions of basic ideas of synthetic differential geometry are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
                ,
                %em Chicago Pizza-Seminar: Synthetic Differential Geometry
                (
                %a{:href => "http://home.sandiego.edu/~shulman/papers/sdg-pizza-seminar.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Lane+Bell"}> John Lane Bell
                ,
                %em An invitation to smooth infinitesimal analysis
                (
                %a{:href => "http://publish.uwo.ca/~jbell/invitation%20to%20SIA.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                R. P. Kostecki,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential Geometry in Toposes
                %a{:href => "http://www.fuw.edu.pl/~kostecki/sdg.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supergeometry"} geometry of physics – supergeometry
